  "as_of": "2022-10-26",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would clarify how the Australian Criminal Intelligence Commission’s board authorises special operations and investigations, simplifying definitions and the wording of its determinations.",
   "It would replace layered criminal activity definitions with clearer crime definitions and expressly connect special operations and investigations to the board’s written authorisations.",
   "The commission’s jurisdiction, investigative powers and existing safeguards would remain, with current determinations, information arrangements and interception warrants preserved through transitional provisions."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "A federally relevant crime definition would identify Commonwealth and territory offences and state offences with a federal aspect.",
   "The relevant crime definition would consolidate past, ongoing and potential future offending.",
   "Related parliamentary oversight and telecommunications interception provisions would use the revised terminology."
  ],
  "affected": "The Australian Criminal Intelligence Commission and its board would be affected.",
